  "question": {
    "text": "If the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> &nbsp;lies inside the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and the circle does not touch or intersect the coordinate axes, then the set of all possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;is the interval"
  },
